Fix for FORTE 3.3.0: a GPIO input line was written when its handle was reset. Deleting a block that
reads a GPIOChip input (a deployment deletes the running resource first) drops its observer, which
resets the handle to FALSE, and the controller wrote that to the input line. The write failed, the
GPIOChip block restarted its controller while the resource was torn down, and FORTE crashed (the
filling Pi, 3 Nov). An input line is now never written. Applied by build-runtime.ps1.

diff --git a/modules/gpiochip/gpiochip_controller.cpp b/modules/gpiochip/gpiochip_controller.cpp
index a58f0eb..3b4a372 100644
--- a/modules/gpiochip/gpiochip_controller.cpp
+++ b/modules/gpiochip/gpiochip_controller.cpp
@@ -170,6 +170,12 @@ namespace forte::eclipse4diac::io::gpiochip {
   }
 
   void GPIOChipController::handleChangeEvent(forte::io::IOHandle *) {
+    if (mConfig.mReadWriteMode == Config::Input) {
+      // An input is read, never written. Its handle is reset (set to FALSE) when its observer is
+      // deleted, e.g. when a deployment deletes the running resource; writing the line then fails
+      // and restarts the controller while the resource is torn down.
+      return;
+    }
     struct gpiohandle_data data{};
     data.values[0] = mValue;
     if (ioctl(mFd, GPIOHANDLE_SET_LINE_VALUES_IOCTL, &data) == -1) {
